---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
    title="A Tern group"
    description="Someone shared a Tern group with you: a join code, which a node takes the group from."
    noindex
>
    <section class="group wrap">
        <div id="found" hidden>
            <p class="label">A group's join code</p>
            <h1 id="name"></h1>
            <p id="unnamed" class="muted" hidden>Whoever made this code gave the group no name.</p>
            <p class="lede">
                Someone shared a Tern group with you. Join it from a node, and you read what its members send
                to it, and can write to it.
            </p>

            <div class="card warn">
                <p>
                    <strong>This code is the group.</strong> Anyone who has it can join and read everything said in
                    the group, before and after, and it cannot be taken back. Pass it on only to those the group is
                    for.
                </p>
            </div>

            <p class="actions">
                <a id="join" class="button" href="/app">Join in the app in your browser</a>
                <button id="copy" type="button" class="secondary">Copy the link</button>
            </p>
            <p id="copied" class="muted small" role="status"></p>

            <p class="muted small">
                The <a href="/app">app in your browser</a> joins from it with a node connected over USB or
                Bluetooth: it asks you first, and the node takes the group. Nothing
                goes on the air: the group's members learn of you only when you write.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div id="missing" hidden>
            <h1>No group here</h1>
            <p class="lede">
                This link does not hold a join code. A join code is the whole link, after the <code>#</code>
                included; check it was not cut short.
            </p>
        </div>

        <noscript>
            <p class="lede">This page reads the join code out of its link, which needs JavaScript.</p>
        </noscript>

        <p class="muted small privacy">
            The code is the part of the link after the <code>#</code>, which a browser never sends to a site. This
            page reads it in your browser and sends it nowhere, so this site learns that a join code was opened, and
            not which group's. It keeps no logs.
        </p>
    </section>
</Base>

<script>
    import "../lib/group/page.ts";
</script>

<style>
    .group {
        padding-top: 32px;
        padding-bottom: 48px;
        max-width: 40rem;
    }
    [hidden] {
        display: none !important;
    }
    h1 {
        font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
        margin: 4px 0 12px;
        overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
    .lede {
        font-size: 1.1rem;
    }
    .label {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        color: var(--muted);
    }
    .card {
        background: var(--surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        padding: 12px 16px;
        margin: 16px 0;
    }
    .card p {
        margin: 0;
    }
    .actions {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 8px;
        margin: 0;
    }
    .small {
        font-size: 0.9rem;
    }
    .privacy {
        margin-top: 28px;
    }
    button,
    a.button {
        display: inline-block;
        font: inherit;
        padding: 9px 16px;
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        border: 1px solid var(--accent);
        background: var(--accent);
        color: var(--bg);
        font-weight: 600;
        cursor: pointer;
        text-decoration: none;
    }
    button.secondary {
        background: transparent;
        color: var(--accent);
    }
</style>
